cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these skills, please cite them."
title: "data-skills: Agent Skills for liberating public data and running public-interest data collaborations"
abstract: "Two portable Agent Skills from the CU Public Interest Data Science (CUPIDS) Lab. data-liberation turns government PDFs, scans, spreadsheets, web pages, APIs and dashboards into tidy, provenance-tracked, reproducible datasets. data-project scopes, governs, tracks, deposits and shares the collaborations around them. Both follow one ten-section outline with checkable outcomes, and generate project artifacts only when the work reaches the section that needs them."
